---Membership contains information about a member cluster.
---@class gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.Membership
---@field updateTime? string Output only. When the Membership was last updated.
---@field lastConnectionTime? string Output only. For clusters using Connect, the timestamp of the most recent connection established with Google Cloud. This time is updated every several minutes, not continuously. For clusters that do not use GKE Connect, or that have never connected successfully, this field will be unset.
---@field endpoint? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.MembershipEndpoint Optional. Endpoint information to reach this member.
---@field description? string Output only. Description of this membership, limited to 63 characters. Must match the regex: `a-zA-Z0-9*` This field is present for legacy purposes.
---@field monitoringConfig? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.MonitoringConfig Optional. The monitoring config information for this membership.
---@field name? string Output only. The full, unique name of this Membership resource in the format `projects/*/locations/*/memberships/{membership_id}`, set during creation. `membership_id` must be a valid RFC 1123 compliant DNS label: 1. At most 63 characters in length 2. It must consist of lower case alphanumeric characters or `-` 3. It must start and end with an alphanumeric character Which can be expressed as the regex: `[a-z0-9]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?`, with a maximum length of 63 characters.
---@field authority? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.Authority Optional. How to identify workloads from this Membership. See the documentation on Workload Identity for more details: https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/how-to/workload-identity
---@field deleteTime? string Output only. When the Membership was deleted.
---@field createTime? string Output only. When the Membership was created.
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.StringMap Optional. Labels for this membership. These labels are not leveraged by multi-cluster features, instead, we prefer cluster labels, which can be set on GKE cluster or other cluster types.
---@field membershipType? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.MembershipMembershipTypeEnum Output only. The type of the membership.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.MembershipState Output only. State of the Membership resource.
---@field uniqueId? string Output only. Google-generated UUID for this resource. This is unique across all Membership resources. If a Membership resource is deleted and another resource with the same name is created, it gets a different unique_id.
---@field externalId? string Optional. An externally-generated and managed ID for this Membership. This ID may be modified after creation, but this is not recommended. The ID must match the regex: `a-zA-Z0-9*` If this Membership represents a Kubernetes cluster, this value should be set to the UID of the `kube-system` namespace object.
---@field clusterTier? gcp.unstable.gkehub_v1.MembershipClusterTierEnum Output only. The tier of the cluster.

